---
const options = [
  {
    name: 'Lock it down',
    verdict: 'and it cannot work',
    body:
      'Every useful action needs a tool you did not allowlist, a package you did not preinstall, a command you have to approve. The agent spends its time asking permission and you spend yours granting it.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Let it loose',
    verdict: 'and it has everything',
    body:
      'Your shell history, your SSH keys, your cloud credentials, your .env files. One prompt injection, one confused tool call, one bad dependency it installed — and the blast radius is your machine and every system it can reach.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="why">
  <div class="page">
    <p class="eyebrow">The trade nobody should have to make</p>
    <h2 class="section__title">There are two ways to run an agent today. Both are bad.</h2>

    <div class="options">
      {
        options.map((option) => (
          <div class="card option">
            <h3 class="option__name">
              {option.name} <span class="option__verdict">{option.verdict}</span>
            </h3>
            <p class="option__body">{option.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <p class="turn">
      Discobox rejects the premise. The constraint does not belong on what an agent
      <em>can do</em> — that is infinitely enumerable, and it is the part you actually
      want. It belongs on what an agent <em>can reach</em>, which is finite, and which
      is exactly one thing.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .options {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .options {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  .option__name {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .option__verdict {
    color: var(--salmon);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .option__body {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.97rem;
  }

  .turn {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.3rem);
    max-width: 60ch;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .turn em {
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--magenta);
  }
</style>
